  "title": "Puddles: Application-Independent Recovery and Location-Independent Data for Persistent Memory",
  "abstract": "In this paper, we argue that current work has failed to provide a comprehensive and maintainable in-memory representation for persistent memory. PM data should be easily mappable into a process address space, shareable across processes, shippable between machines, consistent after a crash, and accessible to legacy code with fast, efficient pointers as first-class abstractions.",
